  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Black Throated Wind** (1 review): Reviewer saw Bobby give it everything live, as if purging something; this doesn't come across on tape [8]\n- **Standing on the Moon** (1 review): Reviewer, who attended, found John's vocal especially sincere and says it captures the mood of the show [8]\n- **Eyes of the World** (1 review): Reviewer hears Mayer playing Eyes of the World hot, but seemingly ahead of the other core members [3]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **feet away dead center**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [10]\n- **Casey Jones with John Popper on Harmonica**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [10]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **DC2015-12-27.DC2015-12-27.DC** (recommended): source not stated; 20 songs; 187 min; rated 3.57/5 by 7 [1]. Said about its sound: Recording is somewhat echoey, especially vocals, but has good fidelity, balanced instruments and vocals, and audible keyboards [5]\n- **DeadCo2015.12.27.audmtx**: source not stated; 19 songs; 187 min [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Audience sounds, including a clapper, are audible on the recording and remind the reviewer of being there [5]\n- Reviewer felt the band took much of the first set to find their sync [6]\n- Reviewer notes many fans were skeptical of John Mayer joining; says he sometimes gets ahead of other members while learning the Dead's vibe [9]\n- Reviewer would prefer hearing him in a Phil and Friends band with Chimenti, maybe JK, and Molo on drums [3]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **DC2015-12-27.DC2015-12-27.DC**: taped by Russell Cansler; transferred by Russell Cansler [1]\n- **DeadCo2015.12.27.audmtx**: Source 1: AT933 through SP12vbb to Sony M-10 at 24/44.1, taped by Russell Cansler; Source 2: Nakamichi CM-700s into Apogee Mini-Me, then Sonosax SX-R4, converted with AudioGate to 16/44, taped by Nakguy [2]",
